'''Infinity 0''' is the input series for a science fiction book about physics and the universe: 495+
pages, currently unedited, written before this project existed. See [[Infinity_0_Interview]] for the
output requirements gathered by [[The_Storyized_Interviewer]]. The raw manuscript text itself, split one
folder per story, lives in <code>core-inputs/input-book/</code> — this page is the status/instructions
side, not the raw content (''SPEC.md'''s "Second concrete case").

== Status ==

* '''State:''' unedited raw draft.
* '''Volume:''' 495+ pages / stories, uncounted precisely — expect this number to be approximate and
  growing.
* '''Ordering:''' unordered for now. The stories don't have a fixed sequence yet, and the sequence may
  change over time as more is understood about how they relate. Don't assume story N comes before story
  N+1 just because of filename or import order. The mechanism for when ordering does start is decided
  (<code>core-inputs/input-book/</code>'s <code>priority.txt</code> — see below) even though no story
  has been assigned one yet.

== Pipeline for this input series ==

This series follows a human-in-the-loop pattern, distinct from an agent going straight from raw input to
finished output:

* The '''input''' is a raw, unedited page or story, as originally written.
* A '''human edit''' pass — not an agent — produces the polished version.
* The edited result is the '''output''' of that pass. Per the wiki-chaining idea in <code>IDEAS.md</code>,
  that output can itself become a new input for whatever downstream processing happens next, rather than
  being a dead end.

In short: for ''Infinity 0'', inputs arrive as the outputs of human edits, not as agent-produced content
being validated by a human. The human is upstream of the agent here, not downstream.

== Open questions ==

* '''Granularity''' — '''resolved''': one story per folder, under <code>core-inputs/input-book/</code>.
* '''Ordering mechanism''' — '''resolved''': a <code>priority.txt</code> file inside each story's
  <code>core-inputs/input-book/</code> folder, containing a single integer. It's authoritative over the
  folder-name number prefix — reordering means editing that file, not renaming the folder.
* '''Edit trigger''' — what starts a human edit pass on a given raw page (manual pick, oldest-first,
  something else), and who performs it?
* '''Completion''' — what marks a given story as "done" — one human edit pass, or several?

